"We are given the following information:\n\n- Bucket C has **9** pieces of fruit.\n- Bucket B has **3 more** pieces of fruit than Bucket C.\n- Bucket A has **4 more** pieces of fruit than Bucket B.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the number of fruits in Bucket B\n\nBucket B has 3 more than Bucket C:\n\n$$\n\\text{Bucket B} = \\text{Bucket C} + 3 = 9 + 3 = 12\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the number of fruits in Bucket A\n\nBucket A has 4 more than Bucket B:\n\n$$\n\\text{Bucket A} = \\text{Bucket B} + 4 = 12 + 4 = 16\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Add the number of fruits in all three buckets\n\n$$\n\\text{Total} = \\text{Bucket A} + \\text{Bucket B} + \\text{Bucket C} = 16 + 12 + 9 = 37\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 37**"
