"Let's solve the problem step by step.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Determine how many buckets each person carried.\n\n- **Eden** carried **4** buckets.\n- **Mary** carried **3 more** buckets than Eden:  \n  $ 4 + 3 = 7 $ buckets.\n- **Iris** carried **1 less** bucket than Mary:  \n  $ 7 - 1 = 6 $ buckets.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Total number of buckets\n\n$$\n4 \\text{ (Eden)} + 7 \\text{ (Mary)} + 6 \\text{ (Iris)} = 17 \\text{ buckets}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Each bucket contains **2 pounds** of sand.\n\n$$\n17 \\text{ buckets} \\times 2 \\text{ pounds per bucket} = 34 \\text{ pounds}\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 34**"
