"Let's solve this step by step.\n\n1. **Winston has 14 quarters.**  \n   - Each quarter is worth **25 cents**.  \n   - So, the total value of the quarters is:  \n     $$\n     14 \\times 25 = 350 \\text{ cents}\n     $$\n\n2. **He spends half a dollar on candy.**  \n   - A dollar is **100 cents**, so half a dollar is:  \n     $$\n     \\frac{1}{2} \\times 100 = 50 \\text{ cents}\n     $$\n\n3. **Subtract the cost of the candy from the total amount.**  \n   $$\n   350 - 50 = 300 \\text{ cents}\n   $$\n\n**Answer: 300**"
