"We are given the following information:\n\n- Lizzie has **half as many crayons as Bobbie**.\n- Bobbie has **three times as many crayons as Billie**.\n- Billie has **18 crayons**.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1:** Find how many crayons Bobbie has.\n\nBobbie has 3 times as many crayons as Billie:\n\n$$\n\\text{Bobbie's crayons} = 3 \\times 18 = 54\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Step 2:** Find how many crayons Lizzie has.\n\nLizzie has half as many crayons as Bobbie:\n\n$$\n\\text{Lizzie's crayons} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 54 = 27\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{27}\n$$\n\n**Answer: 27**"
