"We are given the following information:\n\n- Harper drinks **\u00bd bottle of mineral water per day**.\n- She wants to last **240 days**.\n- Each **case contains 24 bottles** and costs **$12.00**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the total number of bottles Harper needs\n\nShe drinks **\u00bd bottle per day**, so over **240 days**:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total bottles needed} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 240 = 120 \\text{ bottles}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Determine how many cases she needs\n\nEach case contains **24 bottles**, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Number of cases} = \\lceil \\frac{120}{24} \\rceil = \\lceil 5 \\rceil = 5 \\text{ cases}\n$$\n\n(Note: We round up to the next whole number because you can't buy a fraction of a case.)\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the total cost\n\nEach case costs **$12.00**, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost} = 5 \\times 12 = 60\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 60**"
