"We are given the following information:\n\n1. The **lioness** is **12 years old**.\n2. The **lioness's age is twice the age of the hyena**.\n3. The **babies of both animals are half the age of their mothers**.\n4. We are to find the **sum of the ages of the babies in five years**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the age of the hyena\n\nWe are told:\n> The age of the lioness is **twice** the age of the hyena.\n\nLet the age of the hyena be $ H $.\n\nThen:\n$$\n\\text{Lioness's age} = 2H\n$$\nWe are told the lioness is 12 years old:\n$$\n2H = 12 \\Rightarrow H = 6\n$$\n\nSo, the **hyena is 6 years old**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the age of the babies\n\n- The **lioness's baby** is half the age of the lioness:\n  $$\n  \\text{Lioness's baby} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6 \\text{ years old}\n  $$\n\n- The **hyena's baby** is half the age of the hyena:\n  $$\n  \\text{Hyena's baby} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 = 3 \\text{ years old}\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Find the age of the babies in five years\n\n- Lioness's baby in 5 years: $ 6 + 5 = 11 $\n- Hyena's baby in 5 years: $ 3 + 5 = 8 $\n\nSum of the babies' ages in five years:\n$$\n11 + 8 = 19\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 19**"
