"We are given the time it takes for a woman to **drive** and **fly** to a job interview, and we are to find how many **minutes faster** it is to take the **airplane**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Convert all times to minutes for consistency.**\n\n- **Driving time:** 3 hours and 15 minutes  \n  \u2192 3 \u00d7 60 = 180 minutes  \n  \u2192 180 + 15 = **195 minutes**\n\n- **Airplane time:**\n\n  - Drive to airport: **10 minutes**\n  - Wait to board: **20 minutes**\n  - Airplane flight time: **One-third of the driving time**  \n    \u2192 195 \u00f7 3 = **65 minutes**\n  - Get off plane and arrive: **10 minutes**\n\n  So, total **airplane time** is:  \n  10 + 20 + 65 + 10 = **105 minutes**\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Compare the two times**\n\n- **Driving time:** 195 minutes  \n- **Flying time:** 105 minutes\n\nDifference:  \n195 \u2212 105 = **90 minutes**\n\n---\n\n### **Final Answer:**\n\n**Answer: 90**"
