"We are given that Tod drives:\n\n- 55 miles **north**\n- 95 miles **west**\n\nSo, the total distance Tod drives is:\n\n$$\n55 + 95 = 150 \\text{ miles}\n$$\n\nHe drives at a constant speed of **25 miles per hour**.\n\nTo find the total time he drives, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{150}{25} = 6 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n**Answer: 6**"
"We are told that Savannah has **3 rolls of wrapping paper** and uses them to wrap **12 gifts**. The problem gives us the following:\n\n- 1 roll is used to wrap **3 gifts**.\n- 1 roll is used to wrap **5 gifts**.\n- The **third roll** is used to wrap the **remaining gifts**.\n- There is **no leftover wrapping paper**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Determine how many gifts are wrapped with the first two rolls.\n\n- First roll: 3 gifts\n- Second roll: 5 gifts\n\nTotal wrapped with the first two rolls:  \n$$\n3 + 5 = 8 \\text{ gifts}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Total number of gifts is 12.\n\nSo, the number of gifts wrapped with the **third roll** is:  \n$$\n12 - 8 = 4 \\text{ gifts}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{4}\n$$\n\n**Answer: 4**"
"We are given the following:\n\n- Sedrach has **13 apple pies**.\n- Each **apple pie** can be **divided into halves**.\n- Each **half** of an apple pie can be **split into 5 bite-size samples**.\n\nWe need to find how many **people** can **taste** Sedrach's apple pie if he divides them all into bite-size samples.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: How many halves are there from 13 pies?\n\nEach apple pie can be divided into **2 halves**.\n\nSo, from 13 pies:\n\n$$\n13 \\text{ pies} \\times 2 = 26 \\text{ halves}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: How many bite-size samples are there from 26 halves?\n\nEach half can be split into **5 bite-size samples**.\n\n$$\n26 \\text{ halves} \\times 5 = 130 \\text{ bite-size samples}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: How many people can taste the apple pie?\n\nAssuming each person gets **1 bite-size sample**, then the number of people who can taste the apple pie is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{130}\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 130**"
