"We are given the following information:\n\n- Gavin has had **4 dreams every day** this year.\n- He had **twice as many dreams last year** as he had this year.\n- We are to calculate the **total number of dreams** he has had in **two years**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the number of dreams this year\n\nGavin has 4 dreams per day. There are 365 days in a year (assuming a non-leap year).\n\n$$\n\\text{Dreams this year} = 4 \\times 365 = 1,460\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the number of dreams last year\n\nHe had **twice as many dreams** last year as this year:\n\n$$\n\\text{Dreams last year} = 2 \\times 1,460 = 2,920\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Add the dreams from both years\n\n$$\n\\text{Total dreams} = 1,460 + 2,920 = 4,380\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 4380**"
"**Step 1: Calculate Faith's regular weekly hours.**  \nShe works 8 hours per day, 5 days a week:  \n$$ 8 \\times 5 = 40 \\text{ hours} $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate her overtime hours per week.**  \nShe works 2 hours of overtime per day, 5 days a week:  \n$$ 2 \\times 5 = 10 \\text{ hours} $$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate her total hours for the week.**  \n$$ 40 \\text{ regular hours} + 10 \\text{ overtime hours} = 50 \\text{ hours} $$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate her total earnings.**  \nShe earns $13.50 per hour:  \n$$ 50 \\times 13.50 = 675 $$\n\n**Answer: 675**"
"We are given the following information:\n\n- The salesman bought **48 backpacks** for **$576**.\n- He sold **17** backpacks at **$18** each.\n- He sold **10** backpacks to a department store at **$25** each.\n- The **remainder** were sold at **$22** each.\n- We are to find the **profit**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Total cost of the backpacks\n\nThe total cost is given as:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost} = \\$576\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Revenue from sales\n\nWe calculate the revenue from each group of sales:\n\n1. **17 backpacks sold at $18 each:**\n\n$$\n17 \\times 18 = 306\n$$\n\n2. **10 backpacks sold at $25 each:**\n\n$$\n10 \\times 25 = 250\n$$\n\n3. **Remaining backpacks sold at $22 each:**\n\nFirst, find the number of remaining backpacks:\n\n$$\n48 - 17 - 10 = 21\n$$\n\nThen, revenue from these 21 backpacks:\n\n$$\n21 \\times 22 = 462\n$$\n\nNow, total revenue:\n\n$$\n306 + 250 + 462 = 1018\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Calculate profit\n\nProfit = Total Revenue - Total Cost\n\n$$\n\\text{Profit} = 1018 - 576 = 442\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 442**"
