"We are given a problem involving 90 students, and we need to track how many are in the cafeteria and how many are outside after some movement.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Initial Distribution**\n\nThere are **90 students** total.\n\n- **Two-thirds** of the students sat in the **cafeteria**:\n  $$\n  \\frac{2}{3} \\times 90 = 60 \\text{ students in the cafeteria}\n  $$\n\n- The **remainder** (i.e., the other one-third) sat **outside**:\n  $$\n  90 - 60 = 30 \\text{ students outside}\n  $$\n\nSo initially:\n- **Cafeteria**: 60 students\n- **Outside**: 30 students\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Movement of Students**\n\n- **One-third of the students outside** jumped up and ran **inside**:\n  $$\n  \\frac{1}{3} \\times 30 = 10 \\text{ students moved from outside to cafeteria}\n  $$\n\n- **3 students** from the **cafeteria** went **outside** to see what was happening.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Update the Numbers**\n\n- **Cafeteria**:\n  - Start: 60\n  - +10 (from outside): 60 + 10 = 70\n  - -3 (to outside): 70 - 3 = **67**\n\n- **Outside**:\n  - Start: 30\n  - -10 (to cafeteria): 30 - 10 = 20\n  - +3 (from cafeteria): 20 + 3 = 23\n\n---\n\n### **Final Answer:**\n\n**67 students are now in the cafeteria.**\n\nAnswer: 67"
